From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:01:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 65/68] vgpu: enable primitive restart on strip topologies

Metal unconditionally enables primitive restart (0xFFFF for UInt16 and
0xFFFFFFFF for UInt32) on indexed LineStrip and TriangleStrip draws with
no state toggle to disable it. Vulkan leaves primitiveRestartEnable off
by default, which caused multi-quad indexed TriangleStrip batches such
as RenderBox path_exterior_vertex (13 sub-segment quads separated by 12
0xFFFF restart sentinels in a 64-index buffer) to execute vertex 65535
and bridge adjacent quads across the scanline.

Enable primitiveRestartEnable on LineStrip and TriangleStrip graphics
pipelines, matching Vulkan 1.0 core rules without requiring optional
list-restart features.
